 61NI    60NI(D,P),(POL D,P)           1967CO27,2013SC06,1973AY03ENSDF    202006
 61NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=20-Jan-2020$                    
 61NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61NI2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61NI c  No changes made since the 2015 update                                  
 61NI c  1967Co27: (d,p): E=7.5 MeV. Measured |s(E(p),|q), 23 angles (c.m.)     
 61NI2c  from |?7|' to 172|', magnetic spectrograph, enriched target,           
 61NI3c  FWHM=10 keV                                                            
 61NI c  2013Sc06, 2013ScZZ: (d,p), E(d)=10 MeV beam from WNSL-Yale             
 61NI2c  tandem accelerator facility. Measured proton spectra, |s(|q), and      
 61NI3c  spectroscopic factors C{+2}S for 19 proton groups using a split-pole   
 61NI4c  Enge spectrograph. FWHM |?33 keV. Target=204 |mg/cm{+2} thick 99.7%    
 61NI5c  enriched. Deduced levels, J, |p. DWBA analysis. Comparison with        
 61NI6c  shell-model calculations.                                              
 61NI c  The main purpose of the neutron adding and neutron removal reaction    
 61NI2c  studies by 2013Sc06 was to obtain occupancies of neutron orbitals,     
 61NI3c  proton vacancies, and energy centroids of neutron, neutron-holes,      
 61NI4c  proton-single particle excitations in {+60}Ni and {+62}Ni, and thereby 
 61NI5c  investigate closure of 0f{-7/2} shell. Some data details of this study 
 61NI6c  are supplied in 2013ScZZ                                               
 61NI c  Others:                                                                
 61NI c  1964Fu04: (d,p): E=12 MeV. Measured |s(E(p),|q), 7 angles from 5|' to  
 61NI2c  50|', magnetic spectrograph, enriched target , FWHM=10 keV.            
 61NI c  1973Ay03: (pol d,p): E=10 MeV. Measured vector analyzing power,        
 61NI2c  |q(c.m.)|?2.5|'-70|', semi detector and magnetic spectrograph,         
 61NI3c  enriched target.                                                       
 61NI c  For gross structure of |g-spectrum as a function of E(p) in (d,p|g),   
 61NI2c  see 1968Na15.                                                          
 61NI c  1975Ba28 (E=3.0-4.5 MeV, |q(c.m.)|? 10|'-135|',                        
 61NI2c  Levels at 4762, 4907 keV), L-values and S factors.                     
 61NI c  1977St07 (E=2.8 MeV, 23 angles from 50|' to 160|',  FWHM |? 30 keV),   
 61NI2c  22 groups up to 5.3 MeV, |s(|q), L-values and S-factor.                
 61NI c  Other: 1962Co02 (|q=9|',15|',25|',40|'),                               
 61NI c  1991We07: E(d)=2.7, 3.0, 3.3 MeV, FWHM|?22 keV; measured |s(|q), DWBA  
 61NI2c  analysis. Deduced density of valence neutron distributions and         
 61NI3c  density differences between isotopes.                                  
